  "summary": "I wrote the whole scene in `src/main.ts`, but I couldn't check it against the engine or render it. `node_modules/@aura3d/` is empty in this sandbox, so `typecheck` reports only `TS2307: Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'`. That means no type checking happened for any Aura3D call. I also never saw a frame, so the light intensities, bloom, gold look and framing are untested guesses. I wrote the API calls from the docs in `docs/agents/` and the recipe sources.\n\nWhat the scene contains:\n- **Marble pedestal:** four stepped blocks, each finely subdivided. The Carrara pattern is computed per vertex from 3D value noise, with turbulence-warped primary and secondary veins, hairline cracks and soft grey haze. It uses a glossy clear-coated physical material.\n- **Trophy:** the cup, stem and foot are one revolved Catmull-Rom profile in polished gold (metallic, low roughness). Two swept-tube handles are also gold. A raised band with fine grooves on the cup, and a collar on the stem, use darker, rougher gold. The base is black polished stone with a thin gold plate on its front face.\n- **Room and environment:** an enclosed dark warm gallery with bright windows, mullions, warm lamps and a ceiling panel. `environments.capture` bakes that room into the environment probe. If the capture doesn't work, the gold will look dark.\n- **Lighting:** one warm shadow-casting spotlight above and in front, a faint cool fill, a subtle warm rim point light, and light bloom.\n- **Camera:** it orbits ±15° around the trophy, on a 22 s cycle with a phase offset so it is already moving at start. `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { materials: ['marble','gold','darkstone'], cameraAzimuthDeg }` is updated every frame. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nI couldn't find how to move the camera at runtime. The docs only mention `app.camera?.setPose(...)`, so I guessed the argument shape (`position`, `target`, `fov`). If `setPose` is missing or throws, the code rotates the pedestal and t",
